-- title:
--   Public calibrated weights and finite rejection programs
-- statement:
--   The public acceptance weight is evaluated from the finite paired-tensor table. The interface defines the calibrated weight, charge predicate, capped rejection state, and protected-chart metadata. Random-bit inputs and the finite retry count remain explicit, so these operations compose with the public machine program.
